<!--
  B.3 EID-22 pack: a child of stock rule 61650 (Sysmon event 22, a DNS query),
  hand-ported from the Sigma YAML in phase-b-detection/sigma/. Phase B ISA F4.
  ID 100412 here; the other B.3 rules sit in their own pack files.

  How the port reads (each construct is in phase-b-detection/CONSTRUCTS.md):
    - every matcher is pcre2 and case-insensitive, as a Sigma string match is
    - a plain Sigma string is anchored at both ends, |contains is not
    - a value list is one alternation, and a selection that is a list of two
      maps (one exact, one |contains) is one alternation of the two forms
    - "not 1 of filter_*" is a negated field. All twelve filters test Image and
      nothing else, so they join into one negated Image pattern. A filter that
      mixes |startswith and |endswith on Image (edge_2) is one ordered pattern
    - the decoder hands a rule each backslash of a path doubled, so a separator
      inside a path is written \\+ (one backslash or more)
    - the group names nothing a stock if_group matches. On 4.14.9 no stock
      rule attaches to sysmon_event_22 by if_group, so this is the idiom the
      other packs need and costs nothing here
    - the parent is 61650 alone. On 4.14.9 no stock rule has 61650 as a
      parent and none attaches to its group, so there is no level-0 sibling to
      name as a second parent

  NOTE: no stock rule reads a Sysmon DNS event, so nothing upstream of this
  pack names the event 22 fields. 100412 uses win.eventdata.queryName and
  .image. The logtest run of 2026-11-20 decoded both from a real event 22 on
  4.14.9. The names .queryStatus, .queryResults and .user follow the same
  pattern and are not used here, so no case proves them.

  WARN: a negated field does not match when the field is absent. 100412 is
  silent on an event with no Image, where the Sigma rule would alert. Sysmon
  writes Image on every event 22 the lab endpoint logged.

  WARN: what the port drops. Nothing upstream is dropped. The one difference
  is the doubled-separator tolerance above, which lets a path with a repeated
  separator match a filter where Sigma would not.

  Lint: bun tools/sigma-lint.ts. Tests: bun tools/logtest.ts.
-->
<group name="local,eid22_pack,">

  <!--
    SigmaHQ ec82e2a5: a DNS query for an IP lookup service from a process that
    is not a known browser. Two names match whole (www.ip.cn, l2.io) and the
    other forty-one match anywhere in the query name. The filters are the
    browsers, by install path where upstream gives one and by file name where
    it does not (brave, maxthon, opera, safari, seamonkey, vivaldi, whale), so
    a browser started from any other folder is filtered by name and a binary
    called chrome.exe in a temp folder is not.
  -->
  <rule id="100412" level="10">
    <if_sid>61650</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.queryName" type="pcre2">(?i)^(?:www\.ip\.cn|l2\.io)$|api\.2ip\.ua|api\.bigdatacloud\.net|api\.ipify\.org|bot\.whatismyipaddress\.com|canireachthe\.net|checkip\.amazonaws\.com|checkip\.dyndns\.org|curlmyip\.com|db-ip\.com|edns\.ip-api\.com|eth0\.me|freegeoip\.app|geoipy\.com|getip\.pro|icanhazip\.com|ident\.me|ifconfig\.io|ifconfig\.me|ip-api\.com|ip\.360\.cn|ip\.anysrc\.net|ip\.taobao\.com|ip\.tyk\.nu|ipaddressworld\.com|ipapi\.co|ipconfig\.io|ipecho\.net|ipinfo\.io|ipip\.net|ipof\.in|ipv4\.icanhazip\.com|ipv4bot\.whatismyipaddress\.com|ipv6-test\.com|ipwho\.is|jsonip\.com|myexternalip\.com|seeip\.org|wgetip\.com|whatismyip\.akamai\.com|whois\.pconline\.com\.cn|wtfismyip\.com</field>
    <field name="win.eventdata.image" type="pcre2" negate="yes">(?i)\\(?:brave|maxthon|opera|safari|seamonkey|vivaldi|whale)\.exe$|^C:\\+Program Files(?: \(x86\))?\\+Google\\+Chrome\\+Application\\+chrome\.exe$|^C:\\+Program Files(?: \(x86\))?\\+Mozilla Firefox\\+firefox\.exe$|^C:\\+Program Files(?: \(x86\))?\\+Internet Explorer\\+iexplore\.exe$|^C:\\+Program Files \(x86\)\\+Microsoft\\+EdgeWebView\\+Application\\+|\\+WindowsApps\\+MicrosoftEdge\.exe$|^C:\\+Program Files(?: \(x86\))?\\+Microsoft\\+Edge\\+Application\\+msedge\.exe$|^C:\\+Program Files(?: \(x86\))?\\+Microsoft\\+EdgeCore\\+(?:.*\\)?(?:msedge|msedgewebview2)\.exe$</field>
    <description>EID 22 pack: a non-browser process looked up an IP lookup service.</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1590</id>
    </mitre>
  </rule>

</group>
